    "result_text": "Both tests pass. The change is complete. Here's a summary of the full-stack \"mark invoice as paid\" feature I implemented:\n\n**Database** (`V5__invoice_status.sql`)\n- New Flyway migration adding a `status VARCHAR(16) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'UNPAID'` column to `invoices`.\n\n**Server** (OfficeFloor + Spring)\n- `Invoice.java` \u2014 added a `status` field (defaults to `\"UNPAID\"` so newly created invoices start unpaid).\n- `InvoicePay.java` + `rest/api/invoices/{id}/pay.POST.yml` \u2014 new endpoint `POST /api/invoices/{id}/pay` that flips the invoice to `PAID`, saves it, and records one audit line through the `Audit` service: `INVOICE_PAID id=1 amount=100.00`.\n- `TestSupportController.java` (seed path \u2014 app code that evolves with the schema) \u2014 now inserts the `status` column, honoring the fixture's value and defaulting to `UNPAID`.\n\n**Front-end** (additive \u2014 all new files except the sanctioned slot-region wiring)\n- `slots/defs/invoiceRow.ts` \u2014 new `invoice.row` slot region (context: invoiceId, projectId, status).\n- `features/invoices/status.slot.tsx` \u2014 renders the `invoice-status` cell.\n- `features/invoices/pay.slot.tsx` \u2014 renders the `invoice-pay-<id>` button; a mutation that invalidates `['invoices', projectId]` so the row refreshes itself.\n- `features/invoices/queries.ts` \u2014 added `status` to the `Invoice` type and a `payInvoice()` mutation.\n- `InvoicesTable.tsx` \u2014 added the `<InvoiceRow.Slot />` region to each row (the allowed \"add a region\" edit per CLAUDE.md rule 3).\n\nFrontend typecheck passes and both Playwright tests (status transition + audit record) pass.",
